cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Graph Agent Protocol (GAP) software, specifications, or benchmarks, please cite both the software and the reference paper below."
title: "Graph Agent Protocol (GAP): Unified Typed GraphQL-Profile Gateway, Progressive Disclosure, and Zero-Trust Governance for AI Agents"
type: software
version: "0.1.0-rc.1"
date-released: "2026-11-16"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mike/GraphProtocol"
url: "https://github.com/mike/GraphProtocol"
abstract: "GAP is a typed GraphQL-profile protocol and Rust reference gateway unifying heterogeneous APIs, relational/graph stores, code indices, MCP servers, and durable A2A tasks behind three-level progressive disclosure, batched DataLoader federation, wait-free immutable snapshots, deterministic Cedar authorization, and fail-closed schema-drift/rug-pull protection."
keywords:
  - "agent protocol"
  - "GraphQL"
  - "Model Context Protocol"
  - "Agent2Agent"
  - "progressive disclosure"
  - "zero-trust authorization"
  - "Rust"
  - "Cedar"
authors:
